Do not report an identification failure the album's later success settled.

Why: the activity feed took the newest failed identification job as the
library's failure, whether or not the same album was identified right after.
On 2026-10-24 an attempt failed with INPUT_MOVED because Library Management
moved the album's files mid-attempt (09:08:18 UTC); the retry succeeded one
second later, yet the UI kept "Album identification failed - 0 albums
remaining" as "Needs attention" for hours. The failure query now skips a
failed or attention job when a later job of the same album succeeded; a
failure nothing settled is still shown.

Tests: new test seeds a failed job settled by a later success (no failure)
and an unsettled one (shown); it fails without the fix with the settled
job's id. Full library suites: same pre-existing macOS failure set.

Remove when: upstream settles failures by a later success.

